# libultrahand -- the Ultrahand/Tesla overlay library ovl-rommsync draws with.
#
# Pinned as a submodule rather than vendored: it is upstream's code, it is
# updated by moving this pointer, and `git submodule status` is the only place
# a reviewer has to look to see which revision an .ovl was built from. CI
# checks out with `submodules: recursive` (.github/workflows/ci.yml), which is
# what makes the Switch build reproducible off a bare clone.
#
# Pinned at tag v2.5.3 = 856ddbddd796fc4a59ad2e0bf939c5963e6f9dd2
#
# A tag, never a `main` head: upstream calls main "a pre-release... in constant
# revision, unlike the releases" (libultrahand#11), and v2.0.0 changed four
# signatures in ways that still compile (#199). v2.5.3 is the newest tag and
# what Ultrahand-Overlay itself pins. The line above is the only record of the
# tag name -- a gitlink is a bare sha and the library has no version macro --
# so `ctest -R toolchain.submodule` holds the gitlink to it. Moving it:
# docs/DEVELOPMENT.md#the-toolchain-pin.
[submodule "overlay/lib/libultrahand"]
	path = overlay/lib/libultrahand
	url = https://github.com/ppkantorski/libultrahand.git
